# Shape geometry, circle (engine backlog 14/16; DISCREPANCIES `SHAPE-AWARE-GEOMETRY`).
# A circle is drawn with rx=ry=w/2, so a multi-line label needs a diameter
# of at least the label box's diagonal — max(w,h) is not enough and the text
# crosses the curve. Diagonal edges must land on the curve too. Parse model
# unaffected; tools/shape-check.js asserts the geometry.
figdown 0.1 block
node hub "Route\nreflector\nRR1\ncore\nsite" shape=circle
node p1 "Peer 1"
node p2 "Peer 2"
edge p1 -> hub
edge hub -> p2
pin p1 at=(20,20)
pin hub at=(200,140)
pin p2 at=(400,20)
